      "body": "- [x] I, the PR author, have personally reviewed every line of this PR.\n\n## What does this PR do?\n\nRequire `use_layer_wise_distributed_optimizer=True` when `optimizer=\"muon\"` and `use_distributed_optimizer=True`. Previously the emerging-optimizer factory accepted that combination without layer-wise mode and constructed replicated optimizer state, silently ignoring the requested optimizer distribution.\n\nRaise `ValueError` for the invalid configuration after deprecated optimizer names are normalized, preserving `dist_muon` compatibility and validation under `python -O`. Plain Muon without `use_distributed_optimizer` remains supported. Other optimizers are unchanged.\n\n## Validation\n\n- Extend the existing Muon validation and layer-wise tests to cover rejection, explicit layer-wise mode, and the deprecated alias; no new test module or fixtures.\n- Two-GPU focused run of the existing Muon class and optimizer configuration tests: 8 passed per rank.\n- The existing validation test also passed on both GPU ranks with `PYTHONOPTIMIZE=0` and `PYTHONOPTIMIZE=1` after the `ValueError` change.\n- Configured Black, isort, pylint and ruff checks passed. The workstation formatting wrapper requires a newer Git version, so these checks ran directly in the test container. Optional mypy still reports existing factory typing errors.\n- Independent review completed with no blocking findings.\n\nThis validates the optimizer configuration only; it does not inspect independently configured DDP model chunks. No optimizer update rules or checkpoint formats change.\n",
